  "questions": [
    "TestPoolConcurrent asserts nothing about the errors or state after the concurrent Release/Get/Put sequence; whether Release concurrent with Get/Put is safe is unasserted.",
    "TestPoolConcurrent2 asserts nothing; it only waits for goroutines, so behavior under concurrent Get and Close (including errors and Len) is unasserted.",
    "TestPoolConcurrent3 is entirely commented out; the concurrent Close vs Get scenario is left untested.",
    "TestNew only checks the error from newChannelPool and does not assert Len or other fields.",
    "TestPool_Get_Impl uses t.Errorf on Get error then proceeds to type-assert conn, which would be nil if Get errored; the expected behavior in that error case is unspecified.",
    "TestPool_Get asserts errors from the goroutine Get calls via t.Errorf but the final Len assertion message says 'Expecting %d' with InitialCap-1 while comparing to 0, a message/expectation mismatch.",
    "TestPool_Put's error message for the Len assertion passes 1 as the expected value while the condition compares to MaxIdleCap; the intended expected value is ambiguous.",
    "TestPoolWriteRead does not call Put or Release on the pool or connection.",
    "TestPoolConcurrent2 ignores errors from Get and Close and does not verify that connections are closed.",
    "Whether Get returns the exact ErrMaxActiveConnReached sentinel vs a wrapped error is asserted only in TestPool_Get, not elsewhere.",
    "TestPool_Close asserts conns and factory become nil but does not assert closeFac or other fields.",
    "No test asserts the behavior of MaxIdle truncation ordering (which connections are retained), only the final Len.",
    "Whether typed race conditions or data races are checked is not asserted; tests do not use the race detector explicitly."
  ],
  "review_required": true
}
